      fix(go): add Semgrep grammar augmentation (was empty)
      
      The semgrep-go augmentation had its rules block fully commented out, so
      the augmented Go parser was identical to upstream tree-sitter-go and
      rejected every Semgrep pattern construct ($X, $...X, ..., <... e ...>).
      
      Adds:
        - semgrep_metavariable, semgrep_ellipsis, semgrep_ellipsis_metavar,
          semgrep_deep_expression rules
        - extensions of _expression, _statement, parameter_declaration,
          literal_element, field_declaration, method_spec, _field_identifier,
          _type_identifier, function_declaration to thread the new rules
          through the relevant list productions
        - precedence override on implicit_length_array_type to keep '[...]T'
          unambiguous against expression-position '...'
      
      Closes LANG-468 (umbrella), LANG-470 (deep ellipsis), LANG-472
      (composite literals, struct/interface bodies). Adds 14 corpus tests.
      
      Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
